# Atlas Core UI/UX Accessibility Review & Remediation Spec
**Author:** Iris Ito  
**Department:** Design  
**Project:** Atlas Core  
**Produced:** D15 02:15  
**Inputs used:** Business Document (Company Document)  
## Summary

Security-reviewed accessibility audit and component remediation specification for Atlas Core, aligning UI tokens and focus management with WCAG 2.1 AA and internal design governance.

## Deliverable
```
# Project: Atlas Core - Accessibility Pass
Author: Iris Ito (Design Agent)
Classification: Confidential / Internal Use Only

## 1. Context & Governance
Cross-referenced requirements against the provided Business Document: 'Company Document'. This document served as the baseline standard for design token usage, ensuring our SaaS interface adheres strictly to organizational compliance protocols without exposing internal telemetry or unvalidated data attributes.

## 2. Design Token Adjustments
- Text Contrast: Updated primary text token `#5A6270` to `#2C333F` on light surface backgrounds to exceed the 4.5:1 ratio (achieved: 7.2:1).
- Interactive States: Outlined actionable elements with high-visibility 2px solid `#005FB8` focus rings. Maintained distinct 2px offset to avoid clipping within encapsulated containers.
- Color Independence: Removed color-only error indicators across all authentication and face-to-face service booking workflows; added distinct warning glyphs and semantic text.

## 3. Keyboard Navigation & ARIA Patterns
- Focus Traps: Enforced modal dialogs within Atlas Core to restrict focus looping to active panels, preventing background navigation leakage.
- Screen Readers: Applied explicit `aria-labelledby` and `aria-describedby` associations across all custom dynamic components.
- Landmark Verification: Verified semantic HTML5 structure `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<header>`, and `<aside>` to eliminate ambiguity during automated screen reader parsing.

## 4. Verification & Security Controls
- Visual check completed with automated contrast analyzers.
- Verified that no user PII or sensitive system parameters are exposed in aria-label attributes or metadata tags.
```